codex-run-8.log:32:4. (#10) Wind widget: replace the Unicode arrow with a pixel-art arrow sprite/canvas rotated to the wind direction, and give the wind box the same thick border + offset shadow as .hb/#panel.
codex-run-8.log:97:   - Problem: `renderHud()` sets `ui.t[1].hidden = M.practice`. `#sb` is `display:flex; justify-content:space-between` across 3 children (red team / mid / blue team). Removing the blue team from flow leaves only 2 children, so `space-between` shoves the `.mid` block (INNING / practice stats line) all the way to the right edge instead of centering it — visible in `live-v4.png` as "SOLO PRACTICE · 0 IN · 0 On the Board · 0% HIT · 9 THROWS" crammed into the top-right corner, nearly touching the score pips.
codex-run-8.log:137:    - Problem: `#wind-arrow` renders a plain Unicode `↑` in `font:36px/1 sans-serif` — a smooth, anti-aliased system glyph sitting inside an otherwise fully pixelated scene (canvas is `image-rendering:pixelated`, UI font is "Press Start 2P"). The wind box itself also uses a thin flat `2px solid` border, while every other panel/button in the game uses the thick blocky border + offset drop-shadow (`.hb`, `#panel`).
codex-run-8.log:139:    - Fix: draw the arrow as a small rotated pixel sprite (same technique already used for board/bag textures via `pixTex`) instead of a text glyph, and give `#wind` the same border+shadow treatment as `.hb`/`#panel` for visual consistency.
codex-run-8.log:143:11. **`#hud.menu` hiding relies on class name, not a verified-safe allowlist.** (`index.html:35,686`) The rule `#hud.menu > :not(#title){display:none!important}` hides everything *except* `#title` when phase is menu/intro/champion — but `#panel` lives outside `#hud` entirely (`index.html:110`), so it's unaffected either way. This is fine today, but if a future HUD element gets added outside `#hud`, this hiding mechanism silently won't apply to it. Worth a one-line comment in the code noting the invariant ("anything that must hide on menu screens must live inside `#hud`").
codex-run-8.log:145:12. **`#title.gone{opacity:0}` leaves the title's layout box in place but invisible, not removed.** (`index.html:64`) It no longer intercepts clicks (`#hud{pointer-events:none}`) so this isn't a functional bug, but it means screen readers / tab order still encounter an invisible "BACKYARD CORNHOLE" heading during gameplay. Low priority; add `aria-hidden` toggling alongside the `gone` class if accessibility is a goal.
codex-run-8.log:161:20. **Practice-mode goal/stats line is dense and tiny at `.75em`.** (`index.html:83,709`) "0 IN · 0 On the Board · 0% HIT · 9 THROWS" packs 4 stats into one small centered line — readable at 1280px, cramped below ~480px even before the item-2 flex bug is fixed. Consider 2 lines (accuracy stat separate from the throw tally) once item 2 is fixed and the block is centered again.
codex-run-8.log:165:22. **Confetti `burst()` only fires at the hole.** (`index.html:864,868`) "Knocked in" (opponent's bag pushed into the hole) reuses the same hole-position burst, which is correct, but a cancellation-scored "on the board" point gets no particle feedback at all — only text. Minor asymmetry in feedback weight between a 3-point make and a 1-point board hit; could add a smaller/plainer particle puff for board hits if more "juice" is wanted, though this is explicitly optional given the simplicity goal.
codex-run-8.log:167:23. **Career "NEXT UP" card and the in-match HUD both use the purple `#panel` chrome with a `.go` yellow CTA**, which is good for consistency — but the "LET'S TOSS" / "CIRCUIT MAP" buttons are stacked with no visual hierarchy beyond color (same width, same spacing). On the 390px shot (`task5-intro-390.png`) the secondary "CIRCUIT MAP" button is barely distinguishable from the primary CTA at a glance. Consider a smaller/plain style for the secondary action, consistent with how `.hb` already differs from `.go` elsewhere.
codex-run-8.log:169:24. **`#panel{max-width:94vw}` combined with long taunt strings can force a lot of line wraps on 390px width** (`task5-intro-390.png` shows 6+ short wrapped lines in the card body). Not broken, just dense; shortening taunt copy (already short) or increasing line-height slightly at narrow widths would reduce the "wall of text" feel the owner is trying to avoid elsewhere.
codex-run-8.log:175:- The literal bug described in `CLAUDE_REVIEW_NOTES.md` — HUD text overlapping the title on the menu screen — is fixed by the `#hud.menu` CSS rule + `renderHud()`'s class toggle added in commit `42dd814`. I verified this is live in the current `index.html` (matches working tree, no uncommitted diff).
